---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "3D Printing for Business in the UK"
seoTitle: "3D Printing for Business in the UK | RFQs, Repeat Orders & Small-Batch Supply"
description: "Commercial-friendly 3D printing for UK businesses — RFQs, repeat orders, invoices, first-article samples and practical quality checks from a supplier near Cambridge."
image: "/assets/images/og/batch-commercial-mini-scrapers.jpg"
ogImageAlt: "Pastel-coloured branded mini scrapers laid out as a commercial batch order."
faqItems:
  - question: "Do you provide invoices for business orders?"
    answer: "Yes. Bondar Labs can issue invoices for commercial orders. The business page explains how to send an RFQ and what information helps produce an accurate quote quickly."
  - question: "Can you support repeat orders from a fixed specification?"
    answer: "Yes. Once a part, material and workflow are agreed, reorders can be supplied against the same confirmed specification, with revision changes discussed before production starts."
  - question: "Do you offer first-article samples before a larger batch?"
    answer: "Yes. For larger or more sensitive orders, a first-article or pilot sample can be produced before the main run so fit, finish and function can be checked early."
  - question: "Can you work with purchase orders or an NDA?"
    answer: "PO-style ordering can be supported by agreement where it matches the client’s process, and confidentiality can be covered by an NDA or a customer-provided agreement when needed."
  - question: "Can you measure critical dimensions or provide a simple QC report?"
    answer: "Visual QC is standard. Where required, agreed critical features can be measured with precision callipers and documented in a simple measurement report."
  - question: "What if our file is not fully ready?"
    answer: "That is common. Files, rough CAD, photos, sketches and key measurements can all be enough to start. If more work is needed, design support can be folded into the job."
---

